*! ipwadhc 0.3.2  Continuous-time stabilized IPW for time-varying non-adherence (and censoring by death / loss to follow-up)
*! 0.3.2: compact default output (3-4 lines); option detail restores the covariate block, the table of all weight components and the usage advice. Numbers unchanged.
*! 0.3.1: stores the model specification in characteristics _dta[ipwadh_*] (for stcox_ipwadh); nothing else changed.
*! 0.3.0 is UNTESTED in Stata (run test_ipwadhc_terminal.do, then re-run test_ipwadhc.do and test_ipwadhc_variants.do; 0.2.3 passed both).
*! 0.3.0: new option ltfu(varname): loss to follow-up (second, non-death censoring cause) gets its own pair of Poisson models (same predictors as the
*!        death models) and is weighted (IPCW) together with death: _ipw_swc = death weight x loss weight; the parts Ec0 and dC are the SUMS over the causes, so
*!        ipwadh_split / ipwadh_eval need no change.  New option terminal(censor|none): censor (default) = death is informative censoring and is
*!        weighted (needs dead()); none = death is treated as independent censoring (no death weights; dead() is then only checked).
*!        Other terminal-event estimands (composite, while-alive) need no weights of their own: see TERMINAL EVENTS below.
*! 0.2.3: tight Poisson tolerances (1e-12 1e-14 1e-12) are the DEFAULT in every fit; fallback to Stata's defaults (with a note) if the tight fit
*!        fails or does not converge; poissonopts() replaces the defaults entirely.
*! 0.2.2: option poissonopts() passes options (e.g. tolerance(1e-11) ltolerance(1e-13) nrtolerance(1e-11)) to every Poisson fit; warning notes (also in
*!        quiet mode) when poisson uses fewer rows than the stratum has (perfect prediction) or does not converge.
*! 0.2.1: closing advice corrected (stset with time-varying weights must NOT use id() or exit(time .)); header example shows the full
*!        pipeline; new returns r(trunc_lo) r(trunc_hi) when truncate() is used.
*! 0.2.0: zero-length rows are flagged and ignored (no error); all row-neighbour logic works within the usable rows only;
*!        tie-safe sort; parts option (pieces of the weight formula for evaluation inside a row); clearer errors per stratum.
*!
*! IDEA
*!   Input: UNSPLIT episode data, one row per period with constant covariates (a new row at every adherence change and at every
*!   change of a time-varying covariate). Do NOT split at failure times before this command: the rate models must be fitted on the
*!   episodes. Adherence changes, death and loss to follow-up are modelled as piecewise-constant rates (Poisson regression, exposure = row length).
*!   With state s = current adherence, for the usable rows k = 1, 2, ... of a person (left-continuous weights):
*!     log W(end of row k) = sum_{j<=k} -(rate_num_j - rate_den_j) * len_j      [exposure term, adherence]
*!                         + sum_{j<k}  chg_j * log(rate_num_j / rate_den_j)     [jumps at PAST adherence changes only]
*!                         + sum_{c} sum_{j<=k} -(crate_num_cj - crate_den_cj) * len_j   [censoring causes c = death, loss to follow-up]
*!   Inside row k the weight at time t is   log W(t) = E0_k - dA_k (t - time0_k) + J0_k + Ec0_k - dC_k (t - time0_k)
*!   (variables generated by the option parts: E0, J0, dA, Ec0, dC; Ec0 and dC are sums over the censoring causes), which is what the
*!   piece-time evaluation (ipwadh_eval) uses.
*!
*! TERMINAL EVENTS (what to do with death; the estimand changes with the strategy)
*!   terminal(censor)  default. Death = censoring that depends on measured covariates (IPCW). Estimand: rate ratio had nobody died (hypothetical).
*!                     Needs dead(). Assumes death is conditionally independent of the infection process given the death-model covariates.
*!   terminal(none)    no death weights; death ends follow-up as independent censoring. Also the estimand "infections per unit time alive" (while-alive
*!                     rate ratio): the same computation, only the interpretation differs.
*!   composite         (no option needed) define  gen evt = inf | dead  and use  failure(evt)  in ipwadh_split and stset; run ipwadhc with terminal(none).
*!   ltfu(varname)     loss to follow-up is independent censoring unless this option is given; then it is weighted (IPCW) under every strategy.
*!   Ghosh-Lin style (dead persons stay in the risk set) is NOT implemented: it needs the administrative end of follow-up of dead persons (design pending).
*!
*! ROWS THAT ARE IGNORED (weight = missing, no error)
*!   rows outside if/in, rows with missing id/time/adherence/arm, and zero-length rows (time1 == time0; for example withdrawal at
*!   time 0 or a zero-length first episode). stset ignores zero-length rows as well. Rows with time1 < time0 are an error.
*!   Baseline (time-zero) non-adherence is not modelled: everyone starts in the state of the first usable row.
*!
*! TRUNCATION
*!   truncate(plo phi) clips the combined ROW-END weights at the ROW-weighted percentiles of _ipw_sw (Stata _pctile rule).
*!   For the exact split pipeline use truncate() of ipwadh_eval instead (person-time weighted percentiles of the piece weights).
*!
*! EXAMPLE (exact on-treatment analysis, recurrent events)
*!   ipwadhc, id(id) time0(t0) time1(t1) adherence(adh) arm(arm) dead(dead) ltfu(ltfu) ///
*!       stcoxvars(c.age i.male) adhpredictors(i.tsi i.abx c.biomarker) parts replace
*!   ipwadh_split, id(id) time0(t0) time1(t1) adherence(adh) failure(inf) lastonly(dead ltfu)
*!   ipwadh_eval, time0(t0) time1(t1) adherence(adh) truncate(1 99) replace          // creates _ipw_psw and _ipw_pswt
*!   stset t1 [pw=_ipw_pswt] if adh==1, time0(t0) failure(inf)                       // NO id(), NO exit(time .)
*!   stcox i.arm c.age i.male, breslow vce(cluster id)                               // pweights: robust SE; iweights are NOT allowed
*!   Stata refuses time-varying weights together with id() in stset (r(459)); without id() every piece is its own record and the
*!   failure sits on the last piece of its row, so exit(time .) is not needed either.
*!   Quick approximation without splitting (weights at the row ends only):  stset t1 [pw=_ipw_swt] if adh==1, time0(t0) failure(inf)

program define ipwadhc, rclass sortpreserve
    version 15
    syntax [if] [in], ID(varname) TIME0(varname) TIME1(varname) ADHerence(varname) ARM(varname) ///
        [ NUMvars(string) DENvars(string) DEAD(varname) LTFU(varname) TERMinal(string)           ///
          CNUMvars(string) CDENvars(string) BYARM                                                ///
          STCOXvars(string) ADHPredictors(string) CENSORPredictors(string)                       ///
          TRUNCate(numlist min=2 max=2 >=0 <=100)                                                ///
          GENerate(name) REPLACE PARTs NOIsily POISsonopts(string) DETail ]

    if "`terminal'" == "" local terminal censor
    if !inlist("`terminal'", "censor", "none") {
        di as err "terminal() must be censor or none (composite and while-alive analyses need no weights of their own: see the help text in the .ado header)"
        exit 198
    }
    if "`dead'" != "" & "`ltfu'" != "" {
        if "`dead'" == "`ltfu'" {
            di as err "dead() and ltfu() must be different variables"
            exit 198
        }
    }

    marksample touse, novarlist
    markout `touse' `id' `time0' `time1' `adherence' `arm'
    if "`dead'" != "" markout `touse' `dead'
    if "`ltfu'" != "" markout `touse' `ltfu'

    * plain-language covariate lists (see ipwadh_covlists): translated into the advanced numvars/denvars lists
    if "`stcoxvars'`adhpredictors'`censorpredictors'" != "" {
        if "`numvars'`denvars'`cnumvars'`cdenvars'" != "" {
            di as err "use either stcoxvars()/adhpredictors()/censorpredictors() or the advanced numvars()/denvars() options, not both"
            exit 198
        }
        local covq = cond("`detail'" == "", "quiet", "")
        ipwadh_covlists if `touse', arm(`arm') adherence(`adherence') stcoxvars(`stcoxvars') ///
            adhpredictors(`adhpredictors') censorpredictors(`censorpredictors') `byarm' `covq'
        local coxhint "`r(stcox_hint)'"
        local numvars `r(numvars)'
        local denvars `r(denvars)'
        local cnumvars `r(cnumvars)'
        local cdenvars `r(cdenvars)'
    }

    if "`generate'" == "" local generate _ipw
    local nq = cond("`noisily'" == "", "quietly", "noisily")
    local byflag = ("`byarm'" != "")

    if "`cnumvars'" == "" local cnumvars `numvars'
    if "`cdenvars'" == "" local cdenvars `denvars'

    local outs swa swc sw swt
    if "`parts'" != "" local outs `outs' E0 J0 dA Ec0 dC
    foreach s of local outs {
        capture confirm variable `generate'_`s'
        if !_rc {
            if "`replace'" == "" {
                di as err "variable `generate'_`s' already exists; use option replace"
                exit 110
            }
            drop `generate'_`s'
        }
    }

    * --- checks -----------------------------------------------------------
    quietly count if `touse' & !inlist(`adherence', 0, 1)
    if r(N) > 0 {
        di as err "adherence() must be coded 0/1"
        exit 198
    }
    foreach cv in `dead' `ltfu' {
        quietly count if `touse' & !inlist(`cv', 0, 1)
        if r(N) > 0 {
            di as err "`cv' must be coded 0/1 (dead() / ltfu())"
            exit 198
        }
    }
    if "`dead'" != "" & "`ltfu'" != "" {
        quietly count if `touse' & `dead' == 1 & `ltfu' == 1
        if r(N) > 0 {
            di as err "dead() and ltfu() are both 1 on " r(N) " rows: a person ends follow-up by one cause only"
            exit 459
        }
    }
    tempvar len use ord
    quietly gen double `len' = `time1' - `time0' if `touse'
    quietly count if `touse' & `len' < 0
    if r(N) > 0 {
        di as err "time1() < time0() on " r(N) " rows"
        exit 459
    }
    quietly count if `touse' & `len' == 0
    local nzero = r(N)
    quietly gen byte `use' = (`touse' & `len' > 0)
    quietly count if `use'
    if r(N) == 0 error 2000

    * sort: unusable rows first (use == 0), then within person by time; original order breaks exact ties.
    * every by-group below is  by `use' `id'  and every statement carries  if `use',  so ignored rows never act as neighbours
    quietly gen long `ord' = _n
    sort `use' `id' `time0' `time1' `ord'

    tempvar dup
    quietly by `use' `id' `time0': gen byte `dup' = (_N > 1) if `use'
    quietly count if `dup' == 1
    if r(N) > 0 {
        di as err "id and time0 do not uniquely identify usable rows (" r(N) " rows with a repeated time0 within a person)"
        exit 459
    }

    * usable rows must not overlap
    tempvar ovl
    quietly by `use' `id': gen byte `ovl' = (_n > 1 & `time0' < `time1'[_n-1] - 1e-9) if `use'
    quietly count if `ovl' == 1
    if r(N) > 0 {
        di as err "overlapping rows within id (" r(N) " rows)"
        exit 459
    }

    foreach cv in `dead' `ltfu' {
        tempvar bad
        quietly by `use' `id': gen byte `bad' = (_n > 1 & `cv'[_n-1] == 1) if `use'
        quietly count if `bad' == 1
        if r(N) > 0 {
            di as err "rows exist after a person's end of follow-up (`cv'==1); dead() and ltfu() may be 1 only on a person's last row " ///
                "(if you split with stsplit, set it to 0 except on the last piece)"
            exit 459
        }
        drop `bad'
    }

    * --- adherence change indicator (change at the end of the row, among usable rows) ------
    tempvar chg
    quietly by `use' `id': gen byte `chg' = cond(_n < _N, `adherence' != `adherence'[_n+1], 0) if `use'
    quietly count if `chg' == 1
    local nchg = r(N)
    if `nchg' == 0 {
        di as err "no adherence changes found"
        exit 2000
    }

    * --- strata and right-hand sides ---------------------------------------------
    tempvar sa sc
    if `byflag' {
        quietly egen `sa' = group(`arm' `adherence') if `use'
        quietly egen `sc' = group(`arm') if `use'
        local base_a ""
        local base_c "i.`adherence'"
    }
    else {
        quietly gen double `sa' = `adherence' if `use'
        quietly gen double `sc' = 1 if `use'
        local base_a "i.`arm'"
        local base_c "i.`arm'##i.`adherence'"
    }
    local rn_a `base_a' `numvars'
    local rd_a `base_a' `numvars' `denvars'
    local rn_c `base_c' `cnumvars'
    local rd_c `base_c' `cnumvars' `cdenvars'

    * --- adherence-change rates -----------------------------------------------------
    tempvar lan lad
    _ipwadhc_fit `chg' "`rn_a'" `use' `len' `sa' `nq' `lan' "adherence changes, reduced (numerator) model" "`poissonopts'"
    _ipwadhc_fit `chg' "`rd_a'" `use' `len' `sa' `nq' `lad' "adherence changes, full (denominator) model" "`poissonopts'"
    quietly count if `use' & (missing(`lan') | missing(`lad') | `lan' <= 0 | `lad' <= 0)
    if r(N) > 0 {
        di as err "missing or non-positive predicted rates (" r(N) " rows): missing covariates?"
        exit 416
    }

    tempvar e1 j1 ce cj cjl
    quietly gen double `e1' = -(`lan' - `lad') * `len' if `use'
    quietly gen double `j1' = cond(`chg' == 1, ln(`lan' / `lad'), 0) if `use'
    quietly by `use' `id': gen double `ce' = sum(`e1') if `use'
    quietly by `use' `id': gen double `cj' = sum(`j1') if `use'
    quietly by `use' `id': gen double `cjl' = cond(_n == 1, 0, `cj'[_n-1]) if `use'
    quietly gen double `generate'_swa = exp(`ce' + `cjl') if `use'
    label variable `generate'_swa "Stabilized IPW, non-adherence, at row end (continuous time)"
    if "`parts'" != "" {
        quietly gen double `generate'_E0 = `ce' - `e1' if `use'
        quietly gen double `generate'_J0 = `cjl' if `use'
        quietly gen double `generate'_dA = `lan' - `lad' if `use'
        label variable `generate'_E0 "log weight (adherence): exposure term at row start"
        label variable `generate'_J0 "log weight (adherence): jump terms at past changes"
        label variable `generate'_dA "adherence rate difference (numerator - denominator) in the row"
    }

    * --- censoring causes: death (terminal(censor)) and loss to follow-up (ltfu()) ---------------------
    * each cause c has a reduced and a full Poisson model with the same right-hand sides; exposure and rate differences add over the causes
    local cens ""
    local clab ""
    if "`dead'" != "" & "`terminal'" == "censor" {
        local cens `cens' `dead'
        local clab `clab' death
    }
    if "`ltfu'" != "" {
        local cens `cens' `ltfu'
        local clab `clab' ltfu
    }
    local ncens : word count `cens'
    tempvar edt dct ced
    quietly gen double `edt' = 0 if `use'
    quietly gen double `dct' = 0 if `use'
    forvalues k = 1/`ncens' {
        local cv : word `k' of `cens'
        local cl : word `k' of `clab'
        local wh = cond("`cl'" == "death", "death", "loss to follow-up")
        tempvar mn md ed
        _ipwadhc_fit `cv' "`rn_c'" `use' `len' `sc' `nq' `mn' "`wh', reduced (numerator) model" "`poissonopts'"
        _ipwadhc_fit `cv' "`rd_c'" `use' `len' `sc' `nq' `md' "`wh', full (denominator) model" "`poissonopts'"
        quietly count if `use' & (missing(`mn') | missing(`md') | `mn' <= 0 | `md' <= 0)
        if r(N) > 0 {
            di as err "missing or non-positive predicted `wh' rates (" r(N) " rows)"
            exit 416
        }
        quietly gen double `ed' = -(`mn' - `md') * `len' if `use'
        quietly replace `edt' = `edt' + `ed' if `use'
        quietly replace `dct' = `dct' + (`mn' - `md') if `use'
        drop `mn' `md' `ed'
    }
    quietly by `use' `id': gen double `ced' = sum(`edt') if `use'
    quietly gen double `generate'_swc = exp(`ced') if `use'
    if "`parts'" != "" {
        quietly gen double `generate'_Ec0 = `ced' - `edt' if `use'
        quietly gen double `generate'_dC = `dct' if `use'
    }
    local lbl "nothing"
    if `ncens' == 1 local lbl "`clab'"
    if `ncens' == 2 local lbl "death and ltfu"
    label variable `generate'_swc "Stabilized IPW, censoring by `lbl', at row end (continuous time)"
    if "`parts'" != "" {
        label variable `generate'_Ec0 "log weight (censoring): exposure term at row start"
        label variable `generate'_dC "censoring rate difference (num - den, summed over causes), per row"
    }

    * --- combine, truncate ---------------------------------------------------------------
    quietly gen double `generate'_sw = `generate'_swa * `generate'_swc if `use'
    label variable `generate'_sw "Combined stabilized IPW at row end (untruncated)"

    local show swa swc sw
    local wv `generate'_sw
    if "`truncate'" != "" {
        local plo : word 1 of `truncate'
        local phi : word 2 of `truncate'
        quietly _pctile `generate'_sw if `use', p(`plo' `phi')
        local lo = r(r1)
        local hi = r(r2)
        quietly gen double `generate'_swt = min(max(`generate'_sw, `lo'), `hi') if `use'
        label variable `generate'_swt "Stabilized IPW at row end, truncated at p`plo'/p`phi'"
        local show `show' swt
        local wv `generate'_swt
    }

    * --- diagnostics -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    quietly count if `use'
    local nrows = r(N)
    if "`detail'" != "" {
        di
        di as txt "Continuous-time stabilized IPW" _col(44) "rows = " as res `nrows' as txt "  changes = " as res `nchg'
        di as txt "  censoring weights: " as res cond(`ncens' == 0, "none", "`clab'") as txt "   terminal(" as res "`terminal'" as txt ")"
        if "`dead'" != "" & "`terminal'" == "none" di as txt "  note: terminal(none): dead() is only checked; death is treated as independent censoring (no death weights)"
        if "`dead'" == "" & "`terminal'" == "censor" di as txt "  note: no dead(): death (if any) is treated as independent censoring"
        if `nzero' > 0 di as txt "  note: " as res `nzero' as txt " zero-length rows (time1 == time0) ignored: weight missing (stset ignores them too)"
        di as txt "{hline 70}"
        di as txt "  variable" _col(24) "mean" _col(34) "sd" _col(44) "min" _col(54) "max"
        di as txt "{hline 70}"
    }
    foreach s of local show {
        quietly summarize `generate'_`s' if `use'
        if "`detail'" != "" {
            di as txt "  `generate'_`s'" _col(20) as res %9.4f r(mean) _col(30) %9.4f r(sd) ///
               _col(40) %9.4f r(min) _col(50) %9.4f r(max)
        }
        return scalar mean_`s' = r(mean)
        return scalar max_`s'  = r(max)
        if "`generate'_`s'" == "`wv'" {
            local wmean = r(mean)
            local wsd = r(sd)
            local wmin = r(min)
            local wmax = r(max)
        }
    }
    if "`detail'" != "" {
        di as txt "{hline 70}"
        di as txt "Mean of stabilized weights should be close to 1 (row-weighted means can differ)."
        di as txt "Weights are evaluated at each ROW END. For the exact on-treatment analysis (run ipwadhc with option parts):"
        di as txt "  ipwadh_split, id() time0() time1() adherence() failure() lastonly(dead ltfu)   then   ipwadh_eval, time0() time1() adherence() [truncate(1 99)]"
        di as txt "  stset `time1' [pw=_ipw_psw (or _ipw_pswt)] if `adherence'==1, time0(`time0') failure(your failure variable)"
        di as txt "  stcox i.`arm' ..., breslow vce(cluster `id')"
        di as txt "Do NOT use id() or exit(time .) in that stset: Stata refuses time-varying weights with id() (r(459)). pweights give robust SEs; iweights do not."
        di as txt "Quick approximation without splitting (weights at the row ends only):  stset `time1' [pw=`wv'] if `adherence'==1, time0(`time0') failure(...)"
    }
    else {
        di
        di as txt "ipwadhc: " as res %-9.0fc `nrows' as txt " rows, " as res %-7.0fc `nchg' as txt " adherence changes;  censoring weights: " as res cond(`ncens' == 0, "none", "`clab'") as txt " (terminal(" as res "`terminal'" as txt "))"
        if "`dead'" != "" & "`terminal'" == "none" di as txt "  note: terminal(none): death is independent censoring (no death weights)"
        if "`dead'" == "" & "`terminal'" == "censor" di as txt "  note: no dead(): death (if any) is independent censoring"
        if `nzero' > 0 di as txt "  note: " as res `nzero' as txt " zero-length rows ignored (weight missing; stset ignores them too)"
        di as txt "  row-end weight " as res "`wv'" as txt ":  mean " as res %5.3f `wmean' as txt "  sd " as res %5.3f `wsd' as txt "  min " as res %6.4f `wmin' as txt "  max " as res %6.2f `wmax'
        if "`coxhint'" != "" di as txt "  Cox model to use:  " as res "`coxhint'"
        if "`parts'" != "" di as txt "  next: ipwadh_split ..., lastonly(" as res "`dead' `ltfu'" as txt ")  then  ipwadh_eval"
        else di as txt "  (without option parts only the quick row-end approximation is possible; add parts for the exact analysis)"
    }

    * --- model specification, stored in the data for stcox_ipwadh (characteristics survive ipwadh_split / ipwadh_eval / save) ---
    char _dta[ipwadh_version] "0.3.2"
    char _dta[ipwadh_id] "`id'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_time0] "`time0'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_time1] "`time1'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_adh] "`adherence'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_arm] "`arm'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_cens] "`cens'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_byarm] "`byflag'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_rn_a] "`rn_a'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_rd_a] "`rd_a'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_rn_c] "`rn_c'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_rd_c] "`rd_c'"
    char _dta[ipwadh_popts] `"`poissonopts'"'
    char _dta[ipwadh_prefix] "`generate'"

    return scalar N = `nrows'
    return scalar n_zero = `nzero'
    return scalar n_changes = `nchg'
    return scalar n_cens_models = `ncens'
    if "`truncate'" != "" {
        return scalar trunc_lo = `lo'
        return scalar trunc_hi = `hi'
    }
    return local terminal "`terminal'"
    return local censoring "`clab'"
    return local weightvar "`wv'"
end


program define _ipwadhc_fit
    args dep rhs touse len strat nq newvar what popts
    quietly gen double `newvar' = .
    quietly levelsof `strat' if `touse', local(lv)
    tempvar mu
    foreach l of local lv {
        quietly count if `touse' & `strat' == `l' & `dep' == 1
        if r(N) == 0 {
            di as err "no events for the model of `what' in stratum `l' (nothing to estimate: positivity problem or stratum too small)"
            exit 2000
        }
        quietly count if `touse' & `strat' == `l'
        local nstr = r(N)
        * default: tight convergence (nearly flat likelihoods, e.g. sparse deaths, give ~5e-5 error with Stata's defaults);
        * falls back to Stata's defaults if the tight fit fails or does not converge; poissonopts() overrides both
        local po `"`popts'"'
        local usedtight 0
        if `"`po'"' == "" {
            local po "tolerance(1e-12) ltolerance(1e-14) nrtolerance(1e-12)"
            local usedtight 1
        }
        capture `nq' poisson `dep' `rhs' if `touse' & `strat' == `l', exposure(`len') `po'
        if `usedtight' & (_rc | (_rc == 0 & e(converged) == 0)) {
            di as txt "  note: tight Poisson convergence failed for `what', stratum `l'; refitting with Stata's default tolerances"
            capture `nq' poisson `dep' `rhs' if `touse' & `strat' == `l', exposure(`len')
        }
        if _rc {
            local rc = _rc
            di as err "Poisson model for `what' failed in stratum `l' (r(`rc')): too few events, perfect prediction or collinear covariates"
            exit `rc'
        }
        if e(N) < `nstr' {
            di as txt "  note: Poisson model of `what', stratum `l': " as res e(N) as txt " of " as res `nstr' as txt " rows used (perfect prediction: a covariate was dropped together with its rows)"
        }
        if e(converged) == 0 {
            di as err "  warning: Poisson model of `what', stratum `l' did not converge"
        }
        quietly predict double `mu' if `touse' & `strat' == `l', n
        quietly replace `newvar' = `mu' / `len' if `touse' & `strat' == `l'
        quietly drop `mu'
    }
end
